I can't speak for everyone, but here's my $0.02...

This was the first time I was able to find the website for
/dev/null/nethack.  I'd bet a lot of others are in the same sistuation.
 Every post should have had the URL for the site.  I spent a lot of
time on google before I found it.

Once I created a character, there was an inordinatly long time before
the server was ready for me to play.  That right there probably lost a
good chunk of newbies.  I almost gave up myself.

Then came the discovery that 1) not having a light source in a dark
room was an instadeath and 2) you couldn't use the E-word, and 3) the
grue code written so as to take away nethack's philosophy of being able
to check things out like your inventory before moving and possibly
getting killed.   I played a couple of games before I finally decided
to go back to NAO.

Next year I'd suggest using an official version of nethack.  If you
want more challenges get the devteam to add them.  The grue challenge
actually shows promice.  I'd love for there to be something more
interesting in the mines than what is already there.

However the light source requirement needs some work.  Nethack is very
big on letting you think and gather  information before you move.  You
should be able to do that in a dark room too.  In the main branch,
there also needs to be some way around the darkness if you don't have a
light source or a way to dig.  I had one game on dlvl1 where the only
place the downstairs could be was either in a dark room or in a room
beyond the dark room.  I had no way to cross it and no way to get
around it.
One possible solution is to make the the grues into a real monster that
you can fight and flee from.  They should be way higher level than what
would normally be generated and should flee from light and only be
created in dark rooms.

That's just my two cents.

